Job Title
Consumer Marketing Manager Mother & Childcare Benelux

Job Description
Your Challenge:
Grow your consumer marketing & business management skills and own the Mother&Childcare category under the Philips AVENT brand, which is a strategic business for the Benelux country organization of Philips Personal Health.
As market leader, our objective is to grow our Philips AVENT brand by supporting parents and their babies, giving them the best start in life to set the stage for healthier futures. We do this by bringing meaningful innovations, because we believe there is always a way to make life better. As our current Consumer Marketing Manager is moving on to a next challenge, we are looking for an ambitious all round marketing
professional with excellent digital, e-commerce marketing and business management skills to replace her.
Are you passionate about defining the marketing strategy, bringing innovations to the market, developing content-driven activations, including through our own apps Pregnancy+ and Baby+, driving conversion to online and offline sales, and delivering top- and bottom line business results? Then this is your opportunity to lead the category as part of the Philips business in the Benelux.
As Consumer Marketing Manager Mother & Childcare Benelux, you will be part of the broader Philips marketing team, which consist of multiple marketing managers responsible for other Philips categories such as Philips Sonicare, shavers, Philips Lumea etc. In addition to the ownership of the category, you will be responsible for various (digital) marketing processes within the Benelux marketing team to stimulate your development within the organization and business development skills. The Philips AVENT Benelux Personal Health marketing team, which also consists of specialists in different marketing functions such as Digital, Media and PR.

You are responsible for

• Develop and execute effective marketing strategies and activation plans, always with the consumer in mind and focused on long term as well as short term activities, including advertising budget control;

• Responsible for the local activation (including in-app localized content) of the Philips owned apps for Pregnancy+ and Baby+, with an enormous reach within the target audience

• Responsible for local market, competition, shopper and consumer analysis to help you determine your marketing strategy based on the consumer decision journey;

• Manage revenue & margin targets of the Mother & Childcare category in the Benelux market;

• Work as part of the full commercial triangle including Sales and Trade Shopper Marketing;

• Actively work together in the above with the Professional marketing and Key Opion Leader Manager for Mother & Childcare to drive professional marketing for the Philips AVENT brand

• Give direction to and collaborate with a cross-functional category team with digital experts, media, PR;

• Take care of excellent communication & collaboration with both internal and external colleagues, as well as internal and external stakeholders;

• Within the Mother & Childcare marketing team, you are responsible for various (digital) marketing processes, such as digital campaign management and product introduction processes.

You are a part of
The passionate and driven Personal Health Benelux marketing team, which consists of consumer marketing managers responsible for various propositions.
Your base will be in Best, the Netherlands. Additionally, you will regularly visit our Amsterdam office. You report to the Consumer Marketing lead, based in Best.

To succeed in this role, you should have the following skills and experience

• Minimum of 4 years’ experience in marketing management role with category responsibility, experience in developing and executing the marketing strategy with budget responsibility;

• Master’s degree, preferably Commercially / Business oriented;

• Digital marketing experience is a plus;

• Affinity with market trends in B2C marketing environments;

• You take ownership and drive for results by acting as a true business manager;

• Capability to think strategic and act pragmatic and you bring a track record to show it;

• Strong stakeholder management skills, driven by strong communication and interpersonal skills;

• Fluent in both Dutch and English is a must, French is a plus.

Compensation & benefits
Doing meaningful work should come with fair, transparent rewards. The base salary range for this role is €61.185 - €101.976.
We determine pay within the range using objective factors, like the skills the role requires, your relevant experience and the responsibility you'll have in this role, alongside internal equity and local market considerations. This role is eligible for 3% on-target Short Term Incentive with your rewards linked to both individual performance and company results. We’ll share the full approach with you during the interview process, so you can make a clear, informed decision.

How we work together
We believe that we are better together than apart. For our office-based teams, this means working in-person at least 3 days per week.

About Philips
Are you ready to do the work of your life to help the lives of others? Learn more about our business, discover our rich and exciting history and learn more about our purpose.
If you’re interested in this role and have many, but not all, of the experiences needed, we encourage you to apply. You may still be the right candidate for this or other opportunities at Philips. Learn more about our culture of impact with care.
